{
  "id": "hooks/guard/live-text-is-still-a-command",
  "title": "text the shell or another program can run is still judged: substitutions, sh -c and eval, text fed to a shell, the words of a command that is not a data command, and a line the lexer cannot parse",
  "source": [
    "intended: docs/decisions.md, section \"Only launches are blocked, and launches into other repositories\" (the guard denies only what starts an agent)"
  ],
  "intent": "A line that lexes is judged command by command. A substitution is a command of its own. The command string of sh -c, eval and env -S is read as a line, and so is the --command value of orca terminal create. When a command of the line reads its commands from its input (a shell with no -c and no script, source of /dev/stdin, sudo -s, a shell run by xargs), the heredoc bodies, the here-strings and the quoted text of the data commands are read as lines too; when a variable is run as the program, the heredoc bodies and here-strings are. The Orca launch verbs are looked for in the words of every command that is not a data command, so a program that runs one of its quoted words is still judged. A line that does not lex goes to the old splitter.",
  "for_each": {
    "vars": [
      "command",
      "verb"
    ],
    "ids": [
      "substitution-in-double-quotes",
      "backtick-in-double-quotes",
      "substitution-in-an-unquoted-heredoc",
      "echo-of-a-substitution",
      "heredoc-read-by-bash",
      "heredoc-read-by-a-wrapped-shell",
      "heredoc-after-redirections",
      "heredoc-piped-to-sh",
      "heredoc-piped-through-tee",
      "heredoc-in-a-process-substitution",
      "heredoc-in-sh-c",
      "here-string-to-bash",
      "source-reads-a-here-string",
      "echo-piped-to-sh",
      "printf-piped-to-bash",
      "a-group-piped-to-a-shell",
      "xargs-runs-its-input",
      "sudo-s-reads-a-pipe",
      "heredoc-read-into-a-variable-that-runs",
      "sh-c",
      "sh-c-two-commands",
      "eval",
      "env-S",
      "unbalanced-quote",
      "bash-c-worker-start",
      "substitution-as-the-program",
      "substitution-in-sh-c",
      "watch",
      "ssh",
      "tmux",
      "screen",
      "su",
      "parallel",
      "script",
      "find-exec",
      "python3-c",
      "node-e",
      "docker-exec-sh-c",
      "busybox-sh-c",
      "git-c-alias-spaced",
      "git-rebase-exec",
      "quoted-harness-in-a-terminal-command",
      "second-command-of-a-terminal-command",
      "sh-c-after-a-double-dash",
      "case-inside-a-substitution"
    ],
    "rows": [
